    <h2 style="color:var(--primary);margin-top:48px">What makes our robotic surgery team experienced</h2>
    <div class="proof-grid">
      <div class="proof-card">
        <h3>Verified surgical training</h3>
        <p>Dr. Hardik Shah trained in orthopedic surgery in India and earned the <strong>FRCS (Germany)</strong> fellowship; Dr. Swagat Shah holds the <strong>FIAAS (UK)</strong> fellowship in arthroscopy and arthroplasty. Both credentials sit at the senior end of orthopedic specialisation in India.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-card">
        <h3>2,000+ knee replacements performed</h3>
        <p>The DHS knee programme has performed <strong>2,000+ knee replacement surgeries</strong> across robotic and conventional techniques, with high patient satisfaction.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-card">
        <h3>VELYS imageless robotic platform</h3>
        <p>DHS uses the <strong>VELYS Robotic-Assisted Solution</strong> from <strong>Johnson &amp; Johnson DePuy Synthes</strong> &mdash; the fastest-growing robotic knee platform in India since its November 2022 launch. No pre-op CT scan, no extra radiation, real-time ligament balancing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-card">
        <h3>NABH-accredited hospital</h3>
        <p>DHS Multispecialty Hospital is NABH-accredited and supported by 24/7 emergency, ICU, anaesthesia, radiology and physiotherapy &mdash; everything a modern robotic surgery programme needs in one building.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

